# .pii-allow — benign name-shaped strings, pinned exactly, with reasons.
#
# Read by ~/.config/kenning/pii-shape.py. Format: <exact string><TAB><reason>.
# The string is pinned exactly and the reason is required: an allowlist of
# PATTERNS would be a hole, an allowlist of exact facts closes behind itself,
# and a line with no reason is not a ruling but a silencer. Same design as
# .seal-accepted-drift.
#
# Every entry here is a phrase that is name-SHAPED and is not a person. If a
# real name ever needs adding to this file, that is the signal to remediate
# instead.

The Apache License	licence prose in NOTICE
Old Norse	etymology of "kenning" in TRADEMARKS.md
Old English	etymology of "kenning" in TRADEMARKS.md
The Kenning AI	our own mark, in prose
Claude Code	product name, MCP client configuration example
Claude Desktop	product name, MCP client configuration example
The IP	sentence-initial "The IP can change" — HOWTO honesty test
The Session's	sentence-initial possessive in prose
The Cypher	section heading, "The Cypher escape hatch"
List Domains	MCP tool title
List Knowledge Types	MCP tool title
List Connection Types	MCP tool title
Merged Layers	test fixture entity name, not a person
Pydantic Models	source section heading
Namespace The	sentence-initial after a config key in prose
Ali Exmpl	deliberate misspelling of the Alice Example placeholder, illustrating that a reference can be wrong
